 "stem": "Find the value of the following: $\\dfrac{\\cos^2 60^\\circ + \\cos^2 30^\\circ + {=k}\\tan^2 45^\\circ}{{=m}\\left(\\sin 60^\\circ \\tan 60^\\circ - \\sin 30^\\circ\\right)}$",
 "solution": [
  "Numerator: $\\left(\\frac12\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)^2+{=k}(1)^2=\\frac14+\\frac34+{=k}={=k + 1}$.",
  "Bracket: $\\sin 60^\\circ\\tan 60^\\circ-\\sin 30^\\circ=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\times\\sqrt3-\\frac12=\\frac32-\\frac12=1$.",
  "Denominator: ${=m}\\times 1={=m}$.",
  "The value is $\\frac{{=k + 1}}{{=m}}={=t}$."
 ],
 "answer": "t",
 "proposed_misconceptions": [],
 "notes": "Advanced: modelled on book example 1-b. Numerator = 1 + k, bracket = 1, so k = m*t - 1 makes the answer t whole."
}
